===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|camboose}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kəˈbuːs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|uːs|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|cambuse}}, from {{etyl|dum|en}} {{m|dum|kabuys}}, {{m|dum|kabuis}} (Modern {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|kombuis||galley; kitchen}}).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|obsolete|nautical}} A small [[galley]] or [[cookhouse]] on the [[deck]] of a small [[vessel]].
# {{label|en|US|rail transport}} The last [[car]] on a [[freight]] [[train]], having [[cooking]] and [[sleeping]] [[facilities]] for the [[crew]]; a [[guard]]’s [[van]].
# {{label|en|slang|baby-talk|or|euphemistic}} [[buttocks]]
# {{label|en|slang|sports}} The person or team in last place.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|last car on train}} [[guards van]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

